 #uuid "4383ecaa-1c57-5705-8853-cba2341fc9fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-103812" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1].$\n- $y=-1$ is the maximum value of the function.\n- $x=15\\pi $ is in the domain." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ therefore the function doesn't have a maximum value. Hence, statements I and II are both false.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement III is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103812/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103811/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "e61d67e0-b2ea-5d42-9c5b-d5dd15090e74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103811/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "64f5a113-3a93-5f49-a906-264d8e2e4129" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103811/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2a26a132-1541-51f6-bfeb-c1e7fd574f70" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103811/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e25101ff-788d-5793-b8a3-c964b279cd69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103811/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "bf58768a-7a58-5816-87b4-b3839e2d1327" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103811/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa80557c-13ec-5d35-a6ac-fe232a00e958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103811/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-103811/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-103811/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-103811/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-103811/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-103811/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103811" :question/id #uuid "d63e671d-d666-591d-bcdc-e6dce8b04cf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-103811" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\n- The domain of the function is all positive real numbers.\n- $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, the statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi .$ So, $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6\\pi ).$ Hence, statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103811/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103811"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65307/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d08954fd-628f-5eba-995f-ba3d2710998c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65307/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "737d3937-2c60-56b3-9d10-ac94f2ef320b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65307/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "fdfec527-d381-52c9-957f-8e264e9e35c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65307/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "761f856e-7e90-553b-b58a-42945fa39f5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65307/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b51a7a87-7aae-53e0-a04f-f828bb8f4511" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65307/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "65f19d68-e4f0-5c3a-855e-b6da1a0ce440" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65307/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-65307/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-65307/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-65307/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-65307/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-65307/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65307" :question/id #uuid "e3d0e09c-4187-5e59-be64-c2ab267e5341" :question/math-academy-id "q-65307" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers.\n- $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-65307/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f1