nsure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65308" :question/id #uuid "d268d1cb-4840-53b4-9239-94fbc360c111" :question/math-academy-id "q-65308" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\n- The range of the function is all real numbers.\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$\n- $x=5\\pi $ is in the domain of the function." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=1,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement II is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $5\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-65308/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103814/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "da212c45-9a31-5a10-ae17-4cbcf0113812" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103814/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "98752cd8-424d-5e02-b4ce-0fa64f274c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103814/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "30804f63-c71e-5af3-a2d8-4ca485011915" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103814/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "6169b1f9-2f5c-5472-95da-ac7ac922ae81" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103814/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "936af1ed-f3e2-5e3a-9f44-2e9fabb8dff7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103814/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b490ebb-4961-552f-8f50-6a4a8eb39305" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103814/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-103814/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-103814/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-103814/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-103814/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-103814/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103814" :question/id #uuid "5aee14ce-41d0-51b6-96b0-a07b706c537b" :question/math-academy-id "q-103814" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n- $y=1$ is the minimum value of the function. $$\n- $x=9\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- The function takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/066fe6ce8a65927436d64753ec4e61bfea257405e4b2f81554ac8341572bcf15.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )$, therefore the function doesn't have a minimum value. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence statement II is true.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$ Hence statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103814/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103814"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103822/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "c4985d07-3eef-56a8-89dd-d1711128ad59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103822/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "55a52eb5-915c-571c-afd6-5b0f427e7014" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103822/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "fcc5dec9-7f64-5b90-b71b-d6326f72de6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103822/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "e2760f35-3658-5196-9bcc-68d3af32df16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103822/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "58172275-a52c-52ad-a3a0-5afd5bf69abb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103822/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3887d24-25ba-522a-8729-2c7bf051d914" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103822/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-103822/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-103822/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-103822/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-103822/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-103822/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103822" :question/id #uuid "172ea96d-b239-53d5-9f76-8cc24f2c7e3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103822" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=6,$ then what is $\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+16\\pi )+5?$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=8$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot 8\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+16\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=6,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+16\\pi )=6.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+16\\pi )+5 & =\\frac{1}{3}(6)+5 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}+5 \\\\  & =2+5 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103822/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37434c3e-2269-5b08-94c5-7516df7879b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10382