03818" :question/id #uuid "eaa7b309-c8e9-5ca2-a11e-2cdf142dad7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-103818" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=3,$ then what is $5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+12\\pi )?$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot 6\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+12\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=3,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+12\\pi )=3.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+12\\pi )=5\\cdot 3=15.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103818/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37434c3e-2269-5b08-94c5-7516df7879b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103818"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103820/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "0ac5c6a4-7044-5b3e-9710-7cdd04a62bfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103820/selection/ec5d74fdf85299ce51c48ff4d0c4119a3a4b7f5f0c689831a0ca11a97ca62771" :answer/id #uuid "d344d922-4f7c-550c-8223-1b55704399a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103820/selection/3f950f42ac32d3d7d9738c89476ce39be2aa62705af1c0691d3a27fbfffa42e6" :answer/id #uuid "0c78fd9e-315e-55e5-b275-1d1f197f5b0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103820/selection/3c675774aa83075422fb7f45bae94d222fac7f997d1693821b70f9bac666a59c" :answer/id #uuid "a40a5e84-be3a-50ca-9292-61d2d56d6a5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +\\sqrt{5}" :db/en