stion/answer-fields ["q-66605/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37434c3e-2269-5b08-94c5-7516df7879b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66605"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158071/selection/3de79bddf6f841c5881cdae443d3aaa683eb5842e99646c5b7e2837e89382703" :answer/id #uuid "82e0f72f-7a12-538b-8b7c-b1b1ec20e060" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158071/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "44630ec8-1f55-50ca-9893-0b2abb062a92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158071/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "a8f8f874-f2fc-57c8-b581-d72473d1b9c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158071/selection/d5f6764a5cc10e135306591ec4dacb40918fc1a36128d20a9f7bb4063814da66" :answer/id #uuid "8742b659-b4aa-54ec-816a-14ada295b83a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158071/selection/c2724874453e84fa99374647d0694dc238ab831bc6b7d897dc21c9d3c7e61851" :answer/id #uuid "a1cb6a92-f6ea-53eb-adfa-8ff414f97287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158071/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "42304c1a-a61e-5e12-afaf-ad02255c8a13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158071/selection/c2724874453e84fa99374647d0694dc238ab831bc6b7d897dc21c9d3c7e61851" :answer-field/choices ["q-158071/selection/3de79bddf6f841c5881cdae443d3aaa683eb5842e99646c5b7e2837e89382703" "q-158071/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-158071/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" "q-158071/selection/d5f6764a5cc10e135306591ec4dacb40918fc1a36128d20a9f7bb4063814da66" "q-158071/selection/c2724874453e84fa99374647d0694dc238ab831bc6b7d897dc21c9d3c7e61851"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158071" :question/id #uuid "bf38e601-43be-5e7d-af2e-e70a9b611ce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-158071" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{7}{6},$ then $4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x+6\\pi )+1=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/a8e7894ea970c539ca59a73713fa15450f4361b3fc8bc22183e3fe84946411bd.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x)=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x+6\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x+2\\pi \\cdot 3) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x) & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x+6\\pi )+1 & =4(-\\frac{7}{6})+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{14}{3}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-158071/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a710f9-fed1-5fdb-b4c0-fd3ae2d4d8a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158071"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158066/selection/25a170deff842212ed37326913af9f79324c30fcf28877ae81d5293be7b7c870" :answer/