atorname{csc}⁡a=\\sqrt{5},$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-a)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/a8e7894ea970c539ca59a73713fa15450f4361b3fc8bc22183e3fe84946411bd.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x)=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-a) & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡a \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158066/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a710f9-fed1-5fdb-b4c0-fd3ae2d4d8a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158066"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158065/selection/7627fb02fec1c7a865cb3e7797f7ea7835cb8ec3423f266885f8f5d01084e358" :answer/id #uuid "6052eede-4d1b-5d4a-86f6-dd65790a5bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158065/selection/e83a540f3a0c82b4093cb3e2952b7e4cf1d91fdf67a578cdd4c22a4f9debc7d4" :answer/id #uuid "50482116-b579-5f26-8633-600e1f27d278" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158065/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "3741942f-151a-5c5e-aeda-18602137d22c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158065/selection/e4feab3a7179f2a87633c6e7922d72261df298535ed5bf9932c62a0940c0196c" :answer/id #uuid "be91eba8-8726-5194-8fa9-6c46f16f41f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158065/select