n/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-136554" :question/id #uuid "a7dd1e9a-1279-521b-a027-8cbf66ac8bba" :question/math-academy-id "q-136554" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡a=-3,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-a)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/a8e7894ea970c539ca59a73713fa15450f4361b3fc8bc22183e3fe84946411bd.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x)=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-a) & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡a \\\\  & =-(-3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-136554/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a710f9-fed1-5fdb-b4c0-fd3ae2d4d8a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-136554"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158069/selection/f114c855cb4980abfc1057e37678c04cac7ea9d9ad649da669e46dcd5213df25" :answer/id #uuid "7129ab19-d435-59ce-bd90-787e61a68c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158069/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "79af9801-52ba-53ef-8554-91ddef0d29d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158069/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "941f08df-23f7-533b-832a-1e1b40ab03f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158069/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "fc1539a6-12c4-58dd-8101-55be42a83427" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158069/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "2839bb61-47a9-5845-9d3c-f979450ddcad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158069/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be887e9e-ae3f-51c1-8bf7-e3ba846a01c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158069/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-158069/selection/f114c855cb4980abfc1057e37678c04cac7ea9d9ad649da669e46dcd5213df25" "q-158069/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-158069/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" "q-158069/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-158069/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158069" :question/id #uuid "6b51c3cc-4e29-5f27-9745-00205139cdc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-158069" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-4,$ then $3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x-18\\pi )-7=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/a8e7894ea970c539ca59a73713fa15450f4361b3fc8bc22183e3fe84946411bd.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x)=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x-18\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x-2\\pi \\cdot 9) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x) & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x \\\\  & =-(-4) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x-18\\pi )-7 & =3(4)-7 \\\\  & =12-7 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-158069/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a710f9-fed1-5fdb-b4c0-fd3ae2d4d8a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
